    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Hashing</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Set membership</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-consecutive-sequence/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 128</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Longest Consecutive Sequence</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Put the numbers in a hash set and only start counting at a number whose predecessor is missing. Every run is then walked exactly once from its first value, so the total work is O(n) even though there is a loop inside a loop.</p>\n"
  },
